				Lys.
				32.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>B.</b>
			
				Pass.
			 and 
				Med.
			, <i>twist</i> or <i>turn oneself</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρεφθείς</span>
			<i>having turned face upward</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.435
			</span></i>; <i>turn round</i> or <i>about, turn to and fro</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				575
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τε κύνεσσι κάπριος ἠὲ λέων
					στρέφεται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.42
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐστρέφετ᾽ ἔνθα καὶ
			ἔνθα</span>, of one <i>tossing</i> in bed, <i><span class="en">
				24.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δυσκολαίνεις καὶ στρέφει τὴν
				νύχθ᾽ ὅλην</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				36
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Amphis
				20.4
			</span></i>; of patients, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.664
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>turn to</i> or <i>from</i> an object, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμελλε στρέψεσθ᾽ ἐκ χώρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
