				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἄρθροις ς. κοτυληδών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					1495
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>turn</i> or <i>twist about</i>, like a wrestler
			trying to elude his adversary: hence, in argument, <i>twist and
				turn, shuffle</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί ταῦτα
			στρέφει</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				385
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί δῆτα ἔχων στρέφει</span>;
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				236e
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάσας στροφὰς στρέφεσθαι</span>
			<i>twist</i> every way, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>R.</u>
				405c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				302b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>turn and change</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἂν σοῦ στραφείη θυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1134
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρεφόμενα λέγων</span>
